20
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:08,600
are half the story. Ethereum is

21
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:12,320
above all an evolving ecosystem,

22
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:14,280
and these contents will keep

23
00:01:14,280 --> 00:01:17,159
changing as the technology changes

24
00:01:17,159 --> 00:01:20,640
and as the ecosystem's focus

25
00:01:20,640 --> 00:01:23,439
shifts from building basic

26
00:01:23,439 --> 00:01:26,720
infrastructure to now

27
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:28,759
putting a huge amount of focus on

28
00:01:28,759 --> 00:01:32,159
applications. So what is Ethereum?

29
00:01:32,159 --> 00:01:36,479
First, Ethereum is the world computer.

30
00:01:36,479 --> 00:01:38,399
Who here remembers Ethereum being the

31
00:01:38,399 --> 00:01:40,680
world computer?

32
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:43,920
This is where I'm supposed

33
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:45,640
to insert that meme

34
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:47,200
with the astronaut holding a gun,

35
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:49,399
saying "Always has been," but I never

36
00:01:49,399 --> 00:01:51,799
understood why giving someone such an

37
00:01:51,799 --> 00:01:54,399
amazing revelation should

38
00:01:54,399 --> 00:01:56,119
come at the same time as

39
00:01:56,119 --> 00:01:58,200
shooting them in space

40
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:01,159
20,000 kilometers away from home,

41
00:02:01,159 --> 00:02:03,119
