42
00:02:03,119 --> 00:02:05,439
Ethereum is the world computer;

43
00:02:05,439 --> 00:02:08,280
it always has been and always will be.

44
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:11,400
In addition, Ethereum is an

45
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:14,720
incredibly large and diverse on-chain

46
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:17,440
economy.

47
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:21,840
Fortunately, Josh right before me

48
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:24,280
gave an excellent presentation

49
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:26,519
about all the different aspects

50
00:02:26,519 --> 00:02:28,319
of that economy.

51
00:02:28,319 --> 00:02:31,879
Ethereum is also an

52
00:02:31,879 --> 00:02:34,959
incredibly large and diverse global

53
00:02:34,959 --> 00:02:39,159
community, and Josh and the

54
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:41,840
automated intro we saw earlier

55
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:43,879
did a great job highlighting that.

56
00:02:43,879 --> 00:02:47,239
Ethereum is many things.

57
00:02:47,239 --> 00:02:51,080
You're probably also supposed

58
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:53,800
to flash a sign that says "ETH is money"

59
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:56,040
as well, but Ethereum is

60
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:58,239
lots of different things, and if Ethereum

61
00:02:58,239 --> 00:03:01,440
is all of these things at once,

62
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:04,720
how does the world computer work?

63
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:07,280
Here's how I think about it:

64
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:09,959
Layer 1 is the trust machine,

65
00:03:09,959 --> 00:03:13,920
and Layer 2 is the GPU.

66
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:18,519
Layer 1 is the core

67
00:03:18,519 --> 00:03:23,040
Ethereum blockchain, the anchor

68
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:26,319
that keeps the ecosystem

69
00:03:26,319 --> 00:03:28,599
safe and holds it

70
00:03:28,599 --> 00:03:31,439
together. Layer 1 is why

71
00:03:31,439 --> 00:03:34,360
Layer 2s can trustfully talk

72
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:37,400
to each other, and once everything

73
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:40,680
upgrades to stage two, you'll

74
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:42,760
be able to take an asset, issue it

75
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:45,280
on Optimism,

76
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:47,599
move it into a smart contract on Arbitrum,

77
00:03:47,599 --> 00:03:49,840
and do so

78
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:53,319
with zero counterparty risk.

79
00:03:53,319 --> 00:03:58,400
Layer 1 is not there to be ultra-fast;

80
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:01,239
it's not there to do a million transactions

81
00:04:01,239 --> 00:04:03,599
per second. Layer 1 is first and foremost

82
00:04:03,599 --> 00:04:06,200
there to be decentralized, robust,

83
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:08,720
and dependable.

84
00:04:08,720 --> 00:04:13,599
Layer 2 is the GPU,

85
00:04:13,599 --> 00:04:15,920
made up of all of you in this room who are

86
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:18,079
part of any Layer 2. Who here

87
00:04:18,079 --> 00:04:20,239
is part of a Layer 2?

88
00:04:20,239 --> 00:04:24,400
Great. Who here has used a Layer 2?

89
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:27,479
Who has used Layer 1?

90
00:04:27,479 --> 00:04:32,440
Great, we're all users here, so

91
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:35,199
there are lots of these

92
00:04:35,199 --> 00:04:38,440
different GPUs, and Ethereum the

93
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:40,360
world computer stays together

94
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:42,880
because each one of these GPUs

95
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:46,720
is connected to the trust machine

96
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:50,720
through optimistic proof systems,

97
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:56,440
zero-knowledge proofs, SNARKs, STARKs,

98
00:04:56,440 --> 00:04:59,360
Boojum, PlonK, whatever the buzz

99
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:03,280
words are, and all of

100
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:05,639
these systems ensure Layer

101
00:05:05,639 --> 00:05:08,800
1 can trustfully verify what is

102
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:11,080
going on inside Layer 2s, and

103
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:14,720
Layer 2s can also trustfully

104
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:17,880
read what is happening on Layer 1.

105
00:05:17,880 --> 00:05:19,960
There's an important interplay between

106
00:05:19,960 --> 00:05:22,360
these two components, and together they

107
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:24,759
make up the Ethereum we have today.

108
00:05:24,759 --> 00:05:28,240
So what is Layer 1? It's a chain that runs

109
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:31,639
proof of stake and doesn't falter.

110
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:36,479
So what does this mean?

111
00:05:36,479 --> 00:05:40,479
Ethereum Layer 1 is a chain that has

112
00:05:40,479 --> 00:05:44,039
existed altogether for more than nine

113
00:05:44,039 --> 00:05:46,360
years, and it has existed in its

114
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:48,759
current PoS form for a

115
00:05:48,759 --> 00:05:51,400
little over two years. I think

116
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:54,759
one of the really important things for a

117
00:05:54,759 --> 00:05:58,120
base layer is having

118
00:05:58,120 --> 00:06:00,720
clear evidence that you're building

119
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:02,880
on something decentralized,

120
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:05,520
open, robust,

121
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:07,319
and likely to keep those traits

122
00:06:07,319 --> 00:06:11,520
going into the future.

123
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:15,759
Part of that, of course, is being

124
00:06:15,759 --> 00:06:17,639
something that is slow to change,

125
00:06:17,639 --> 00:06:19,800
not something that will suddenly

126
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:21,599
wake up on a Tuesday

127
00:06:21,599 --> 00:06:23,720
with new management that

128
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:26,520
suddenly decides it's going to

129
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:28,960
start deleting a

130
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:30,880
whole bunch of applications, change its

131
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:33,400
entire model, and push fees

132
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:35,240
up by a factor of ten

133
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:37,720
without warning. Another part of

134
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:40,319
decentralization and resilience is

135
00:06:40,319 --> 00:06:43,360
recovery, so whenever a

136
00:06:43,360 --> 00:06:45,840
problem starts to arise

137
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:48,560
you can recover from it and

138
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:51,479
have a way to improve the

139
00:06:51,479 --> 00:06:54,280
qualities of Layer 1 over time.

140
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:57,160
Over here on the left is a

141
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:59,960
